{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"50a2182944bf717f68e832e035ecac82ce22521b65316526d93f2fa9e474079c","digest":{"component_or_area":"identity authentication and documentation","key_entities":["docs/identity.md","docs/adr/0045-authenticated-identity.md","in-toto Statement","DSSE payloadType","application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json","git-commit-ancestry","keyring schema","snapshot ledger schema","verify-authorship gate","verify-signature gate","scripts/check_docs_index.py"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","design mismatch","identity authentication","in-toto","key validity","ledger schema","verdict vocabulary"],"propositions":["docs/identity.md and ADR 0045 describe an outdated HLC-epoch and raw-bytes design that contradicts the approved in-toto + git-commit-ancestry implementation.","The approved authorship design uses in-toto Statement with DSSE payloadType application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json, binding event_uuid and content_hash.","Key validity is determined by git-commit-ancestry — keyring entries bind public_key to added_at and revoked_at KEY event positions, with an event valid iff its introducing commit descends added_at_commit and not revoked_at_commit.","The snapshot ledger schema is {event_uuid, content_hash, signature, signer_pubkey, position} where position is nested {commit_sha, position}, supporting ledger-only verification of compacted events.","The verify-authorship verdict vocabulary includes verified, unsigned, unknown-author, bad-signature, and key_not_valid_at_era, with display grouping of verified vs. unverified(bad-signature|key_not_valid_at_era|unknown-author).","Documentation must be rewritten to match TS1/TS2/TS3 implementation and pass docs-index completeness validation without obsolete language."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785823760127668044,"uuid":"f62d6231-ccb6-4351-8153-3e55111b03f7"}